<article class="env-definition" id="0ERJ">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ERJ">Definition <span data-tag="0ERJ">82.26.1</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0EDT" data-tag="0EDT">82.2.1</a> let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of good algebraic spaces over $B$. Let $p \in \mathbf{Z}$. A <em>bivariant class $c$ of degree $p$ for $f$</em> is given by a rule which assigns to every morphism $Y' \to Y$ of good algebraic spaces over $B$ and every $k$ a map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  c \cap - : \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ k(Y') \longrightarrow \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _{k - p}(X')  \]
</div>
  <p> where $X' = Y' \times _ Y X$, satisfying the following conditions </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
if $Y'' \to Y'$ is a proper morphism, then $c \cap (Y'' \to Y')_*\alpha '' = (X'' \to X')_*(c \cap \alpha '')$ for all $\alpha ''$ on $Y''$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
if $Y'' \to Y'$ a morphism of good algebraic spaces over $B$ which is flat of relative dimension $r$, then $c \cap (Y'' \to Y')^*\alpha ' = (X'' \to X')^*(c \cap \alpha ')$ for all $\alpha '$ on $Y'$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
if $(\mathcal{L}', s', i' : D' \to Y')$ is as in Definition <a href="/tag/0ER1" data-tag="0ER1">82.22.1</a> with pullback $(\mathcal{N}', t', j' : E' \to X')$ to $X'$, then we have $c \cap (i')^*\alpha ' = (j')^*(c \cap \alpha ')$ for all $\alpha '$ on $Y'$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> The collection of all bivariant classes of degree $p$ for $f$ is denoted $A^ p(X \to Y)$. </p>
</article>